#
# This test is put under comment because sporadic issue have been noticed during CRT runs.
# Those issues (DL data volume receive below expected) occur at a rather high frequency but are not systematic.
# After looking at AP side, the issue is related to a call drop because of overlapping/mismatch RLC windows
# This test has no really added value from a functional pov, and is also run in FR1.
# So, after discussion it was decided to put it under comment and removed from QC/CRT.
#
#[1]5GC001347_B_31_various_QAM_DL traffic in FR2 with DMRS
#    [Documentation]                 expected_dl_volume: Expected data volume value after test execution
#
    # 15 Mbps for 7 mn => 15000000*7*60/8 = 787500000
#   &{test_params}                  Create Dictionary       band_domain=mmW
#   ...                                                     dl_tput=15
#   ...                                                     expected_dl_volume=787500000
#   ...                                                     tl_topology=classical
#
#    TC_1347_DL_ADDITIONAL_DMRS_WITH_SEVERAL_MCS             ${test_params}

[1][1.0] 5GC001347_A_32_various_QAM_UL traffic in FR2 with DMRS
    [Documentation]                 expected_ul_volume: Expected data volume value after test execution

    # 5 Mbps for 5 mn + 20 s => 5000000*(5*60 + 20)/8 = 200000000
    &{test_params}                  Create Dictionary       band_domain=mmW
    ...                                                     ul_tput=5
    ...                                                     expected_ul_volume=200000000
    ...                                                     tl_topology=classical

    TC_1347_UL_ADDITIONAL_DMRS_WITH_SEVERAL_MCS             ${test_params}
